From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 23:10:24 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: implement single-texel buffer alignment

Metal needs a texture buffer to start at its own alignment, so a view that
starts anywhere else is described as a texture that starts up to one
alignment earlier, texel_offset texels in front of the view, and every
buffer-image and texel-fetch coordinate is moved forward by that offset.

Metal then bounds-checks against that wider texture rather than the view,
so a coordinate in [-texel_offset, -1] would read and write the texels in
front of the view. Each coordinate is therefore checked against the view's
element count first, unsigned so a negative one fails as well, and one
outside the view becomes ~0, which lies outside any texture: the read
returns zero and the write is dropped, as robustBufferAccess2 requires. A
test reads, fetches and writes one texel in front of, one past and one
inside a view that starts one texel into its buffer.
---
